      "summary": "Solid first cut with high confidence on origin, size, culture, and invasive status (all backed by UF/IFAS and Kew). The Malpighiaceae oil-bee pollination angle is genuinely documented at family level, and Galphimia's partial departure from that system is peer-reviewed. The skipper/duskywing larval host note is hedged 'probable' by the nursery source, so I kept larval_food false and flagged it in notes. Toxicity is low-confidence — no authoritative source confirms or denies; treated as Green with a plain caveat.",
